# Vantage

Per-deal AI agent for HubSpot. Monorepo at C:\Users\gohje\vantage-hackathon. Frontend always http://localhost:3000. API http://localhost:8000.

## Structure
- `apps/web` — Next.js 15 App Router frontend (port 3000)
- `apps/api` — FastAPI backend (port 8000)
- `packages/mcp-server` — MCP tools for deal intelligence

## API client (do not break)
- All frontend API calls go through `apps/web/src/lib/api.ts`
- Keep `accountsApi`, `draftsApi`, `signalsApi` method signatures unchanged unless explicitly asked
- Dev auth: `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_BYPASS_TOKEN` in `apps/web/.env.local` matches `DEBUG_BYPASS_TOKEN` in `apps/api/.env`

## UI design system
- Neutrals: `zinc-*` only (migrate any `gray-*` to `zinc-*`)
- Primary actions: `bg-zinc-900 text-white` — not indigo gradients
- No `Sparkles` icons for AI labels; use subtle text badges or nothing
- No `bg-gradient-to-*` hero banners; use white cards with left border accents
- Reuse classes from `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`: `.card`, `.section-header`, `.btn-accent`, urgency dots
- Font: Inter (already configured)

## Demo
- Demo account: `python scripts/seed_demo_account.py` in `apps/api` (Meridian Ops)
- Do NOT run agents on the 9 seeded showcase accounts — it replaces MEDDPICC state
- Remove or hide "Simulate" / "Sample" buttons — pre-seed data instead for demo trust
- Trigger agents: War Room "Run Agent" or `POST /v1/accounts/batch-refresh`

## Scope discipline
- One page per agent session when possible
- Extract components from large files instead of growing them
- No drive-by refactors outside the requested page

## Dogfood checkpoint (2026-06-27)

Expert AE walkthrough. Scores: expert rep **7/10**, first-time **5/10**, 3-min judge demo **8/10** (right path).

### What works
- **Today** split panel (queue + detail) is the right home; auto-select first deal; top-7 finite queue
- Draft review: full body, Approve/Decline + training categories, `J`/`K`/`E`/`D` shortcuts
- **War Room**: Act / Intelligence / History; MEDDPICC; Outlook send after approve
- **Watchtower**: signal clusters + $ at risk + weekly trend
- **⌘K** command palette; **Forecast** override flow

### P0 — fix before demo
1. **`4d` on Today deal cards** = pending drafts count, NOT days (`inbox/page.tsx` ~L120). Deal Book correctly says "4 drafts".
2. **Default queue is urgency-first** — #1 can be 0 drafts while #2 has 4. With pending drafts, default to **Drafts** tab or banner ("19 drafts waiting").
3. **Run Agents** toast says "queued" with no completion signal — add done state + auto-refresh (signals/drafts counts).
4. **Help widget stale** (`help-assistant.tsx`) — documents old Agent Inbox (Actions/History/Pipeline), not current Today UI.

### P1 — expert friction
5. Nav overlap: Today / Deal Book / War Room / Watchtower / Intelligence / Analytics — Intelligence overlaps Watchtower+Analytics; demote or merge.
6. **Assistant missing from desktop navbar** (only in unused mobile sidebar).
7. War Room header button overload (Chat, Generate, Run Agent, Brief, Share, Refresh).
8. Approve on Today ≠ Send — Outlook send only in War Room; need post-approve CTA.
9. **MorningBrief** built (`morning-brief.tsx`) but not mounted on Today.

### P2 — polish
10. Naming: "Run Agents" (nav) vs "Run Agent" (War Room) vs "Sweep" (code) — pick one.
11. Urgency % lacks tooltip/legend vs health score.
12. Visual drift: Today=zinc, Deal Book=gray/indigo, Watchtower=indigo.
13. Analytics is manager-first — consider role-gating or demoting from primary nav.

